    <description>ALF-RS-04 FR6: fires directly off the Appraisal record&apos;s own AF_ApprovalStatus__c field changing to Pending (RecordAfterSave, ISCHANGED). Submits into AF_AP_Appraisal_Manager, which routes to the AF_Q_UsedCarTeam queue as approver (2026-09-08 decision - the BRD&apos;s own Assumption 1 says &quot;trade-in approval authority matrix to be provided by the business&quot;, so neither a Sales Manager hierarchy nor the Used Car Team queue is BRD-mandated; user explicitly chose the queue as approver, since the Used Car Team is the persona already closest to the trade-in valuation). This also permanently removes the MANAGER_NOT_DEFINED failure mode hit live earlier - a queue has no Manager-field dependency at all. Notifies every queue member via Custom Notification when a new approval request enters the queue. IMPORTANT CORRECTION 2026-09-08: an earlier version of this flow (and this description) called the approval-requested notification a &quot;BRD gap fix&quot; - re-reading FR1-FR11 literally, that was wrong. FR6 only says &quot;route the trade-in valuation through an approval workflow before it is accepted&quot; and never mentions notifying the approver; FR10 is a SEPARATE, already-correctly-built requirement to notify the New Car Sales Rep once the Used Car Team submits their evaluation (not the same as approver notification). The Custom Notification here is a reasonable real-world addition (a queue member needs to know work has arrived) but was never actually asked for by the BRD - it should not be characterized as closing a BRD-specified gap.</description>
